## v1.0.0b2
+ Add runtime support for `lhcb_ap_datalist` tasks.
  - Generate `lbapi_key.json` from the deposited `config.local.json` APD token.
  - Use `docker://celebichrono/lhcb-apd:0.9.0` container for AP tasks.
  - Run `apd-login` before the AP dataset query.
  - Strip `root://eoslhcb.cern.ch/` prefix from returned paths.
+ Auto-enable Kerberos for any task that has an `lhcb_ap_datalist` predecessor.
+ Treat finished `lhcb_ap_datalist` tasks as inputs when used by downstream tasks to avoid re-running.
+ Add CVMFS repository support.
  - Read `cvmfs` list from `celebi.yaml`.
  - Emit `cvmfs="..."` in Snakefile rule resources.
  - Add workflow-level `resources.cvmfs` to the uploaded `reana.yaml`.
+ Add runner management endpoints.
  - `PATCH /update-runner/<runner>` to update runner settings.
  - `GET /runners-config` to return full runner configurations.
+ Add SSH runner backend for remote workflow execution on generic SSH hosts.
  - Upload job definition files, inputs, and rawdata to the remote host over SFTP.
  - Run Snakemake on the remote host over SSH and poll for completion.
  - Download outputs, logs, and engine logs back to Yuki Storage.
+ Fix SSH runner input/rawdata staging.
  - Copy staged input and rawdata files directly to `imp<short>/stageout/` on the remote host.
  - Remove the unused `stage_manifest.json` path that only worked for the local backend.
+ Fix workflow backend-type resolution on reload.
  - Persist `backend_type` in the workflow's local `config.json`.
  - Correct the workflow config lookup path to include `<project_uuid>/<uuid>`.
+ Fix SSH workflow status update to read job list from local `jobs_info` instead of the remote-only `workflow_info.json`.
+ Store completed jobs with the legacy status `finished` (musical `coda`) so the client displays `[coda][finished]`.
  - Migrate existing workflows that stored the raw musical name `coda` to `finished` on the next status poll.
+ Add unit tests for SSH workflow upload, status update, and backend-type persistence.
+ Bump version to 1.0.0b2.
